# No addresses yet: review falls through to ../../OWNERS. See that file.
#
# What this directory needs from a reviewer is different from what the rest of
# the overlay needs, and the difference is worth writing down.
#
# Every file under lib/ is bytes this project did not write and cannot read.
# Three things have to be true of a change here and none of them is visible in a
# diff: the artifact is the one its coordinate names, the terms recorded in
# README.chromium are the terms it actually carries, and the version agrees with
# the Dagger pin in gradle/libs.versions.toml that the Gradle build resolves. The
# `files` lane checks the first mechanically against vendor/dagger.txt. The second
# is a legal reading and belongs to whoever owns decision 0027. The third is a
# pin bump, which TOOLCHAIN.md governs.
#
# So: a change that adds, removes or replaces a jar is a vendoring review, not a
# build review, and it wants a reviewer who will open README.chromium rather
# than only BUILD.gn. There is no per-file rule saying so, because the reviewer
# is a role this repository has not named yet — naming one is an M0 item, the
# same way ../../android/OWNERS records it for the island's attachment points.
